But I do know they have the remarkable ability

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:11.719
to revivify necrotic tissue.

00:34:12.099 --> 00:34:15.059
So why is it that all the subjects suffer from the same liver disease?

00:34:15.659 --> 00:34:18.340
The cells in the liver are the most resilient cells in the body.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:22.400
I want you to relax, Adam.

00:34:23.199 --> 00:34:24.559
It's me, Dr. Tang.

00:34:38.360 --> 00:34:39.400
What's wrong with him?

00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:42.059
He's deteriorating.

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:45.679
I told your father not to rush the serum's development,

00:34:46.460 --> 00:34:47.239
but he wouldn't listen.

00:35:04.380 --> 00:35:06.119
I don't think it's going to get much cleaner.

00:35:08.260 --> 00:35:09.980
What brings you to the far reaches of the town?

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:10.300
Ellen.

00:35:10.940 --> 00:35:12.980
Well, I thought I might be able to find a clue

00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:14.460
to the former tenant's whereabouts.

00:35:17.260 --> 00:35:17.659
Why?

00:35:18.059 --> 00:35:18.659
He's gone.

00:35:19.280 --> 00:35:20.139
That's what's important.

00:35:23.179 --> 00:35:25.119
You wouldn't happen to know where he is, would you?

00:35:25.400 --> 00:35:25.760
No.

00:35:26.900 --> 00:35:28.800
I just want to forget that he ever lived here.

00:35:29.559 --> 00:35:30.739
Yeah, I can see that.

00:35:31.980 --> 00:35:32.380
Lana.

00:35:34.179 --> 00:35:35.760
Is there something you're not telling me?

00:35:35.760 --> 00:35:36.159
No.

00:35:38.860 --> 00:35:39.300
No.

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:41.139
Of course not.

00:35:46.480 --> 00:35:49.099
I guess I'm going to have to put all this stuff in storage.

00:35:59.099 --> 00:35:59.739
Look.

00:36:04.519 --> 00:36:05.920
I want you to know

00:36:05.920 --> 00:36:09.300
if you ever feel like talking about Adam,

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:11.320
I'm always here.

00:36:16.480 --> 00:36:17.000
Lex.

00:36:19.760 --> 00:36:21.599
Why are you still interested in him, anyway?

00:36:25.780 --> 00:36:28.519
He came to me and asked if I can get him out of your life.

00:36:29.239 --> 00:36:31.519
I'm just following up and making sure he stays that way.

00:36:31.519 --> 00:36:31.559
Here.

00:36:34.900 --> 00:36:39.519
You don't know by now.

00:36:40.000 --> 00:37:00.000
Hey, um, thanks for the lift.

00:37:00.119 --> 00:37:02.079
I think I can take it from here.

00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:04.639
Easy, Jonathan. The doctor said to stand slowly.

00:37:04.639 --> 00:37:07.099
If I stand any slower, I'll be standing still.

00:37:07.519 --> 00:37:09.820
Thank you so much for everything. Bye-bye.

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:12.699
Hey, Clark.

00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:15.780
It's all right, son. The doctor says that...

00:37:15.780 --> 00:37:17.860
The worst of this is behind me.

00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:24.179
Hey, Clark?

00:37:27.099 --> 00:37:28.179
What's bothering you, son?

00:37:31.559 --> 00:37:34.179
When I went to pick up the vial for Vince, Lex was there.

00:37:34.340 --> 00:37:36.039
He was talking to one of the scientists.

00:37:36.739 --> 00:37:39.860
From their conversation, it sounds like Lionel Luther's behind all of it.

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:40.420
I don't know.

00:37:42.199 --> 00:37:43.960
Now, why doesn't that surprise me?

00:37:44.679 --> 00:37:46.960
Dad, when that serum got close to the kryptonite bomb,

00:37:47.019 --> 00:37:48.460
it reacted the same way as my blood.

00:37:51.099 --> 00:37:53.000
So you're saying the serum...

00:37:53.539 --> 00:37:56.880
I know. It sounds crazy, but I think that Lionel Luther's

00:37:56.880 --> 00:37:59.320
found a way to use my blood to bring people back to life.

00:38:03.840 --> 00:38:05.880
If my blood can save lives,

00:38:06.539 --> 00:38:08.320
maybe I should come forward.

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:12.440
What if there's something inside me that could repair Dad's heart?

00:38:12.880 --> 00:38:13.320
Permanently?

00:38:13.820 --> 00:38:14.199
Clark.

00:38:16.099 --> 00:38:17.699
Your mother and I both know

00:38:17.699 --> 00:38:20.360
that you are going to save a lot of lives in this world.

00:38:22.260 --> 00:38:23.800
Even more than you have any idea.

00:38:26.840 --> 00:38:29.139
The only life I'm interested in saving is yours.

00:38:31.019 --> 00:38:31.659
You do.

00:38:33.239 --> 00:38:35.539
You save my life every day that you're with us.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:44.500
And we wouldn't trade that for a single moment without you.

00:38:53.900 --> 00:38:54.340
Hey.

00:38:58.480 --> 00:39:00.039
Hey. How's your dad feeling?

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:02.039
Oh, you never know. He just had a triple bypass.

00:39:02.360 --> 00:39:05.039
My mom actually bought the doctor a combat helmet as a thank you gift.

00:39:05.579 --> 00:39:08.219
Your dad could survive surgery during a siege.

00:39:08.219 --> 00:39:08.340
Thank you.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:14.079
I talked to Garrett's uncle. He wanted to know what happened.

00:39:15.500 --> 00:39:16.300
What'd you say?

00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.699
I couldn't explain Vince's resurrection,

00:39:19.380 --> 00:39:20.840
but I told him that Garrett was a good kid.

00:39:22.119 --> 00:39:23.539
You know, he was desperate.

00:39:24.079 --> 00:39:25.699
He wanted to do whatever he could to save his brother.

00:39:26.360 --> 00:39:28.260
You should have said something about Adam sooner.

00:39:29.239 --> 00:39:30.440
I feel so guilty.

00:39:30.820 --> 00:39:31.900
None of this was your fault.

00:39:32.320 --> 00:39:35.820
Still, I let him threaten me to silence.

00:39:36.840 --> 00:39:38.539
Because you knew it would put people in danger.

00:39:39.119 --> 00:39:39.940
I understand.

00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:41.300
Keeping secrets for that reason.

00:39:42.320 --> 00:39:44.200
It was really hard keeping it from everyone.

00:39:45.500 --> 00:39:46.980
It was kind of a relief to tell you.

00:39:52.980 --> 00:39:54.440
Lana, no matter where we stand,

00:39:54.920 --> 00:39:56.559
I'm still your friend.

00:39:56.880 --> 00:39:58.179
And you can tell me anything.

00:40:02.240 --> 00:40:03.639
You know, that goes both ways.

00:40:03.639 --> 00:40:04.639
I love you.

00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:11.280
I can't do this all alone,

00:40:11.800 --> 00:40:12.880
but I can also make you go,

00:40:12.880 --> 00:40:14.539
and I'll make you run away.

00:40:15.119 --> 00:40:16.099
Wait, Lena...

00:40:16.099 --> 00:40:16.480
You can't cut this.

00:40:16.920 --> 00:40:17.740
You know I'll always keep you as my son,

00:40:17.740 --> 00:40:18.920
just like you did with popeye.

00:40:19.559 --> 00:40:20.720
いや, estoy members.

00:40:22.400 --> 00:40:23.900
We'll just have to get through it together out there.

00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:26.059
You have to sing for my sake.

00:40:28.039 --> 00:40:29.079
Clark.

00:40:32.840 --> 00:40:34.440
What do you think was in that serum?

00:40:34.440 --> 00:40:36.280
What, through the avianONG?

00:40:36.900 --> 00:40:37.820
Dear me.

00:40:37.820 --> 00:40:38.240
Dubious himself.

00:40:38.240 --> 00:40:39.059
Mad Kate.

00:40:39.059 --> 00:40:39.300
I have questions?

00:40:39.300 --> 00:40:39.579
Boys who don't trust her.

00:40:39.579 --> 00:40:39.780
This is important stuff.

00:40:39.780 --> 00:40:39.920
You just need it. nichts deeper.

00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:40.780
Yeah.

00:41:09.940 --> 00:41:39.920
I'm sorry.

